# One line ending everywhere: LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Why this file exists. core.autocrlf=true was handing Windows a CRLF working
# tree while the repository stored LF, and nothing kept the two halves of the
# build in step: _build/partials/ was CRLF, _build/pages/ was mostly LF, and
# build.js concatenates them verbatim — so every page in guide/ came out with
# both endings in the same file.
#
# That is not cosmetic. A multi-line search-and-replace written with "\n" finds
# nothing in a CRLF file and reports zero matches instead of an error, so an
# edit silently does nothing. It has already cost us a run.
#
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf for anyone who clones this repo, so the setting
# travels with the code instead of living in one machine's git config.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Formats git should never inspect or rewrite.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.docx  binary
